===persian===

دلِ شب بود و باران بود و مهتاب
تن و پیراهنش از آب بی‌تاب
کنارش رفتم از عطرِ تنش مست
نشستم مثل آتش بر لبِ آب
دههٔ ۱۳۷۰

===machine===

It was the heart of night, and rain, and moonlight,
her body and her dress restless with water;
I went to her side, drunk on the scent of her,
and sat down like fire on the lip of the water.
The 1370s

===lantern===

It was the heart of the night, and rain, and moonlight;
her body and her dress were restless with the water.
I went to her side, drunk on the scent of her,
and sat down like a fire on the water's lip.

The 1370s

===translation===

===footnotes===

A rhymed quatrain in the classical manner, dropped in among the free verse — one of a
handful in this part of the book. The Persian rhymes مهتاب / بی‌تاب / آب on the same syllable
three times; the English keeps the shape and lets the rhyme go.
